{"gene":"ERBB2","uniprot":"P04626","proteinName":"receptor tyrosine-protein kinase erbB-2 isoform a precursor","function":"Protein tyrosine kinase that is part of several cell surface receptor complexes, but that apparently needs a coreceptor for ligand binding. Essential component of a neuregulin-receptor complex, although neuregulins do not interact with it alone. GP30 is a potential ligand for this receptor. Regulates outgrowth and stabilization of peripheral microtubules (MTs). Upon ERBB2 activation, the MEMO1-RHOA-DIAPH1 signaling pathway elicits the phosphorylation and thus the inhibition of GSK3B at cell membrane. This prevents the phosphorylation of APC and CLASP2, allowing its association with the cell membrane. In turn, membrane-bound APC allows the localization of MACF1 to the cell membrane, which is required for microtubule capture and stabilization","pathwayComment":null,"pathways":[{"id":"R-HSA-422475","name":"Axon guidance","evidence":"TAS","depth":3,"top":false},{"id":"R-HSA-2219530","name":"Constitutive Signaling by Aberrant PI3K in Cancer","evidence":"TAS","depth":4,"top":false},{"id":"R-HSA-9634285","name":"Constitutive Signaling by Overexpressed ERBB2","evidence":"TAS","depth":4,"top":false},{"id":"R-HSA-9734767","name":"Developmental Cell Lineages","evidence":"TAS","depth":2,"top":false},{"id":"R-HSA-9734779","name":"Developmental Cell Lineages of the Integumentary System","evidence":"TAS","depth":3,"top":false},{"id":"R-HSA-9924644","name":"Developmental Lineages of the Mammary Gland","evidence":"TAS","depth":4,"top":false},{"id":"R-HSA-5663202","name":"Diseases of signal transduction by growth factor receptors and second messengers","evidence":"TAS","depth":2,"top":false},{"id":"R-HSA-8863795","name":"Downregulation of ERBB2 signaling","evidence":"TAS","depth":4,"top":false},{"id":"R-HSA-9665230","name":"Drug resistance in ERBB2 KD mutants","evidence":"TAS","depth":4,"top":false},{"id":"R-HSA-9665737","name":"Drug resistance in ERBB2 TMD/JMD m